# vehje-lower. Design

The lowering stage the pre-round surface lacked. After the retirement of
"codegen" as one word for three operations, lowering (constant folding, common-
subexpression elimination, and macro expansion) is its own operation: it
rewrites the program, where checking discharges the judgment and emission
produces target output. Folding it into either would re-fuse what the design
deliberately split.

Lowering has two strata along one seam. The cheap runtime subset ships now and
is what serves the authoring and templating majority, whose speed concern is the
compile stage and the emit. The heavier dev-time equality-saturation e-graph is
deferred (it is the flagged original research) and lands behind the same fold
interface, so nothing downstream changes when it arrives.

## The lowering entry and its strata

- `Lower`. The stage entry: it takes a `LowerStrategy` and rewrites the IR in
  place through the arena, returning the new root. The strategy is where the two
  strata plug in, so a caller chooses the cheap subset or (later) saturation
  without the stage changing shape.
- `LowerStrategy`. The strategy the entry dispatches on: `Cheap` ships now;
  `Saturate` is the deferred dev-time e-graph stratum (named in BACKLOG, the
  variant reserved so its arrival is additive).

## The cheap subset (ships now)

- `Rewrite`. The caller-lent remap side-table (`NodeRef` to `NodeRef`) the
  redirecting rewrites populate, so a rewrite shares or folds by recording a
  redirect rather than mutating the arena. `Rewrite::resolve` follows the remap
  to a node's current representative, and the lowered root is the root resolved.
  No allocation: the region is caller-provided, like `Resolution` and
  `GradeTable`.
- `ConstFold`. A bounded single bottom-up pass that folds an operation whose
  operands are all statically known to a literal. The Core-level fold that needs
  no family operation is an `If` whose condition is a literal boolean, folded to
  its taken branch (recorded as a redirect in the `Rewrite`); folding a primitive
  operation over literal operands waits on the family payload encoding, so the
  `If`/condition fold is the Core fold today.
- `Cse`. Common-subexpression elimination by hash-consing over `vehje-ir`'s one
  `StructuralHash`: a subtree that hashes equal to an earlier one is redirected
  (in the `Rewrite`) to that earlier one, so repeated structure is shared rather
  than recomputed. Its benefit is node-count reduction, not per-op time (an
  optimising backend already removes the recompute), which is exactly what keeps
  a load-time artifact from bloating.
- `Anf`. The output normal form is A-normal form: every intermediate is named
  and evaluation order equals binding order, so effect order is explicit in the
  residual and no separate sequencing form is needed. Hoisting intermediates
  into fresh `Let` bindings creates new nodes, so `Anf` lands with the
  mutable-arena rewrite path (the redirecting `Rewrite` cannot create nodes); it
  is the deferred piece of the cheap subset.
- `RuleTable`. The fixed rule set the cheap subset applies, and the crate's
  validated-data slice: the same table `vehje-runtime-gen` packages for the
  runtime's load-time lowering of arriving scripts, so the Rust crate is the
  definition and the Zig stage is the specialised execution.

## Macro expansion as handler dispatch

- `MacroExpand`. Macro expansion is a compile-stage-effect operation the compile
  stage handles, one instance of the handler discipline rather than a separate
  mechanism. A macro is a rewrite handled at the compile-stage handler; its
  effect is discharged here, so the residual carries no unexpanded macro.
  Expansion is IR-to-IR and creates nodes, so like `Anf` it lands with the
  node-creating mutable-arena path (a catamorphism, not a redirecting `Rewrite`,
  which cannot create nodes), iterated to a fixpoint. The expansion runs over
  host-provided allocation spaces; the framework adapts to N of them (a single
  caller-lent arena the default hypothesis, the count a bench-decided fork
  carrying the `NodeRef` branding decision), never allocating itself.

- Recursive macros are supported. Termination is binding-time well-foundedness,
  in three layers: stage well-foundedness terminates the stage dimension; a
  within-stage per-operation productivity condition, carried as data on
  `vehje-signature`'s operation schema, terminates same-stage recursion; and a
  budget-as-diagnostic (a deterministic named error at arena exhaustion) is
  distinct from passthrough at the family-expansion seam, so exhaustion never
  reads as a truncated program. Above that, a host-configurable recursion
  depth-cap safety backstop (default 255) is always present as the hang-guard,
  and static cyclicity detection on the typestate layers over it as the primary
  mechanism where a sketch proves it feasible (a feasible detector never removes
  the always-on cap). Every refusal here is a first-class diagnostic: the
  construct, the rule, and the fix, span-linked. The terminator is binding-time
  well-foundedness, never a fuel cap as semantics (a cap-decided residual is the
  non-determinism the round killed).

## Non-scope

- The dev-time equality-saturation e-graph (deferred, BACKLOG).
- The check pass's proof discharge (`vehje-check`); lowering reads the grade
  annotations check writes, it does not compute them.
- Output generation (`vehje-codegen`).

## Dependencies

`vehje-ir` for the IR, the structural hash, and the grade annotations;
`vehje-fixpoint` for the relational engine the later saturation stratum queries;
`arvo` and `notko` for the primitives. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.
